5
00:00:12.997 --> 00:00:15.373
YOLO family. Detection is classification
plus

6
00:00:16.623 --> 00:00:19.263
localization, repeated for every object.
The metric

7
00:00:19.263 --> 00:00:21.903
that grades a box is intersection over

8
00:00:22.637 --> 00:00:26.677
union — the overlap between prediction and
ground truth, from

9
00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:30.717
zero to one. Its smarter cousins, G-I-O-U,
D-I-O-U, and C-I-O-U,

10
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.700
add penalties for distance and aspect
ratio, and as a loss they converge faster

11
00:00:37.081 --> 00:00:39.883
than plain L2 on boxes. Most detectors
start

12
00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:44.402
from anchor boxes — prior shapes tiled
across the image at

13
00:00:45.565 --> 00:00:47.904
varied scales and ratios. Each anchor

14
00:00:48.403 --> 00:00:52.240
predicts an offset, an objectness score,
and a class. Running

15
00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:56.894
k-means on your ground-truth boxes finds
good priors, and stacking anchors

16
00:00:57.693 --> 00:01:01.240
across a feature pyramid handles multiple
scales. Newer anchor-free detectors

17
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.440
like FCOS and CenterNet skip this step
entirely. Any detector

18
00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:10.928
produces a flood of overlapping boxes, so
you clean them up with

19
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:15.350
non-maximum suppression. Sort by
confidence, keep the top

20
00:01:15.793 --> 00:01:18.249
box, and drop anything that overlaps it

21
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:23.834
too much. Soft-NMS decays scores instead
of deleting, and DIoU-NMS is a modern

22
00:01:24.696 --> 00:01:27.520
refinement — tune the threshold per
dataset. The

23
00:01:27.915 --> 00:01:30.645
YOLO family made all of this real-time.

24
00:01:31.105 --> 00:01:32.795
It predicts on a grid

25
00:01:33.898 --> 00:01:36.341
in a single pass, with a head

26
00:01:36.911 --> 00:01:39.079
that emits objectness, class, and box

27
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:43.282
offsets together. Versions three through
eight trade blows on speed

28
00:01:44.144 --> 00:01:47.576
and accuracy, and you can export any of
them

29
00:01:47.949 --> 00:01:51.880
to TFLite or ONNX for mobile and edge. To
grade the

30
00:01:52.991 --> 00:01:56.194
whole system, use mean average precision.
Compute the area

31
00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:59.885
under each class's precision–recall curve,
then average across

32
00:02:00.311 --> 00:02:01.789
classes — at I-O-U

33
00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:06.716
zero-point-five for VOC, or averaged
across thresholds for COCO. Always report
it

